    {
      "schema_version": 6,
      "book_id": "PHM",
      "chapter": 1,
      "chapter_usfm": "PHM.1",
      "version_id": 90,
      "version_abbr": "LEB",
      "verses": [
        {
          "verse": 1,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.1",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Paul, a prisoner of Christ Jesus, and Timothy our brother, to Philemon, our dear friend and fellow worker,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 2,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.2",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "and to Apphia our sister, and to Archippus our fellow soldier, and to the church in your house."
        },
        {
          "verse": 3,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.3",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ."
        },
        {
          "verse": 4,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.4",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "I thank my God, always making mention of you in my prayers,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 5,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.5",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "because I hear about your love and faith which you have toward the Lord Jesus and for all the saints."
        },
        {
          "verse": 6,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.6",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "I pray that the fellowship of your faith may become effective in the knowledge of every good thing that is in us for Christ."
        },
        {
          "verse": 7,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.7",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "For I have great joy and encouragement from your love, because the hearts of the saints have been refreshed through you, brother."
        },
        {
          "verse": 8,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.8",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Therefore, although I have great confidence in Christ to order you to do what is proper,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 9,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.9",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "instead I appeal to you because of love, since I am such a one as Paul, now an old man and also a prisoner of Christ Jesus."
        },
        {
          "verse": 10,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.10",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "I am appealing to you concerning my child whom I became the father of during my imprisonment, Onesimus."
        },
        {
          "verse": 11,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.11",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Once he was useless to you, but now he is useful to you and to me,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 12,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.12",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "whom I have sent back to you himself, that is, my heart,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 13,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.13",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "whom I wanted to keep with me, in order that he might serve me on behalf of you during my imprisonment for the gospel."
        },
        {
          "verse": 14,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.14",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "But apart from your consent, I wanted to do nothing, in order that your good deed might be not as according to necessity, but according to your own free will."
        },
        {
          "verse": 15,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.15",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "For perhaps because of this, he was separated from you for a time, in order that you might have him back forever,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 16,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.16",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "no longer as a slave, but more than a slave, a beloved brother, especially to me, but how much more to you, both in the flesh and in the Lord."
        },
        {
          "verse": 17,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.17",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "If therefore you consider me a partner, receive him as you would me."
        },
        {
          "verse": 18,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.18",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "But if in anything he has caused you loss or owes you anything, charge this to my account."
        },
        {
          "verse": 19,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.19",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "I, Paul, write this with my own hand: I will pay it back, lest I mention to you that you owe me even your very self besides."
        },
        {
          "verse": 20,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.20",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Yes, brother, I ought to have some benefit of you in the Lord; refresh my heart in Christ."
        },
        {
          "verse": 21,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.21",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Confident of your obedience, I am writing to you because I know that you will do even beyond what I say."
        },
        {
          "verse": 22,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.22",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "At the same time also, prepare a guest room for me, for I hope that through your prayers I will be restored to you."
        },
        {
          "verse": 23,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.23",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Epaphras, my fellow prisoner in Christ Jesus, greets you,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 24,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.24",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "and so do Mark, Aristarchus, Demas, and Luke, my fellow workers."
        },
        {
          "verse": 25,
          "usfm": "PHM.1.25",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "The grace of the Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit."
        }
      ],
      "verse_count": 25,
